Privacy Policy for MindRush
Last Updated: October 23, 2026

TLL Developers ("we," "our," or "us") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how your information is collected, used, and shared when you use MindRush: Daily Brain Puzzles (the "App").

By using the App, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.

1. Information We Collect

A. Information You Provide to Us
Optional account data: You can play without providing a name or email. If you choose to create an account (or link your anonymous account), you provide an email address, a password and a nickname (display name). The password is handled by Firebase Authentication and is not visible to us. The nickname is optional (it defaults to "Anonymous") and may be shown to other players in the rankings, so please do not use your real name if you do not want it displayed.

B. Information Created by Your Use of the App
User ID: When you open the App, we use Firebase Authentication to create an anonymous account. This assigns you a unique Firebase User ID (uid) that identifies your progress.

Game data: We store in Cloud Firestore your User ID, nickname (if any), email (if you created an account), account creation and last activity dates, high scores, daily streaks, points and the result (date and score) of each daily challenge you play.

C. Information Collected Automatically
Device and advertising identifiers: Google AdMob and Firebase may read your device's Advertising ID, app-set ID, Firebase installation ID and Firebase Cloud Messaging token.

Usage and diagnostic data: Firebase Analytics collects automatically generated events about how you use the App (for example first open, sessions and screens viewed). Google AdMob collects your interactions with ads and diagnostic information such as app launches and crash rates.

Approximate location: Google AdMob derives a general (approximate) location from your IP address in order to serve ads. The App does not request location permission and does not access your precise location.

2. How We Use Your Information
To provide the App: to create and maintain your account, save your progress, track streaks and show the rankings.
To improve the App: to understand usage trends and fix problems (Firebase Analytics).
To show advertisements: to keep MindRush free, we display banner, interstitial and rewarded ads through Google AdMob. AdMob also uses the data it collects for ad measurement, analytics and fraud prevention.
To send notifications: the App asks for permission to show notifications and registers with Firebase Cloud Messaging, for example for Daily Challenge reminders. You can refuse or turn them off in your device settings.

3. Third-Party Services and Data Sharing
We use the following services from Google. Their own privacy policies apply to the data they process:

Google AdMob (advertising): receives and uses, for its own purposes of advertising, ad measurement and fraud prevention, your Advertising ID and other device identifiers, your interactions with ads, diagnostic information and your approximate location (from the IP address). This is the only third party with which data is shared for its own purposes.
Google Mobile Ads / AdMob policy: https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads
Google Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy

Firebase (Authentication, Cloud Firestore, Analytics, Cloud Messaging, Cloud Functions): backend services that process data on our behalf, such as accounts, game data, usage analytics and notifications.
Firebase privacy information: https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy

We do not sell your personal data. The App does not use Firebase Crashlytics, Google Play Games or in-app purchases. All data is transmitted encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS).

4. Data Retention
We keep your account and game data (User ID, nickname, email, scores, streaks and challenge results) in Cloud Firestore for as long as your account exists, until you ask us to delete it. Anonymous accounts are tied to your installation: if you uninstall the App or clear its data you may lose access to your progress. Data processed by Google AdMob and Firebase Analytics is kept according to Google's policies.

5. Deleting Your Account and Data
The App does not currently include a delete-account button. To request deletion of your account and its associated data (User ID, nickname, email, scores, streaks and challenge results):
- Use the request page: https://tlldevelopers.github.io/PRIVACY_POLICIES/mindrush/delete-account/
- Or email tll.developers.apps@gmail.com from the address linked to your account (or include your User ID, if you play anonymously).
We delete the account and its data within 30 days of receiving your request. Deletion is permanent. You can also reset or delete your Advertising ID in your device settings (Settings > Google > Ads).

6. Your Rights
Depending on your location (for example under the GDPR or CCPA), you may have the right to access, correct or delete your personal data, and to object to or limit certain processing. To exercise these rights, contact us at the email below.

7. Children's Privacy
MindRush is not directed to children under 13 and is not designed for children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has provided us with personal data, contact us and we will delete it.

8. Security
We rely on the security measures of Google Cloud Platform and Firebase, including encryption in transit. However, no method of transmission over the internet or of electronic storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

9. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will post the new version on this page and update the "Last Updated" date above.

